Interactive render delegate edits through a UsdImagingGL.Engine, from python

A sphere in front of the camera is rendered by the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate, driven by a headless
UsdImagingGL.Engine as a viewport does, see testsuite/common/interactive_engine_test.py. Its material color is
changed twice, it moves out of the frame while Arnold is still rendering the second change and comes back, and the
depth AOV is rendered before switching back to the color. Each render is checked in test.py, and the last one is
compared against the reference image.

author: cyril.pichard@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'script': '"{}" test.py'.format(usd_python)}
